    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1975-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The sequence begins \\[ 1,3,2,-1,-3,-2,1,3,\\ldots \\] and repeats every \\(6\\) terms, with period sum \\(0.\\) The first \\(96\\) terms sum to \\(0,\\) and the last four sum to \\(1+3+2-1=5.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Generate terms until the initial pair \\(1,3\\) returns",
        "The six-term period has sum \\(0\\)"
